# ORCLDEV: devices whose animation and scheduling ride CurrentTick (M16.4).
#
# This is the scenario that exercises the phase solver. Vanilla runs
# `CurrentTick := Random(100)` when it enters a GamePlayLoop (GAME.PAS:1515) and
# again when the player unpauses (GAME.PAS:1564), and three of this world's four
# devices draw straight off that value:
#
#   Clockwise conveyor  CurrentTick / 3 % 4      (glyph period 12)
#   Counter conveyor    CurrentTick / 2 % 4      (glyph period 8)
#   Spinning gun        CurrentTick % 8          (glyph period 8)
#   Transporter         CurrentTick / 2 % 4      (glyph period 8)
#
# The periods deliberately disagree, so one phase has to satisfy all four at
# once — a shifted or off-by-one draw mapping in any single element cannot be
# absorbed by choosing a different phase.
#
# The conveyors are ringed with a boulder, a gem, and ammo so their tick moves
# real tiles rather than only animating, which also makes the CYCLE GATE
# observable: `CurrentTick mod Cycle = statId mod Cycle` decides which of the two
# conveyors turns on which frame, so the phase is behavioural here, not cosmetic.
# The gun carries p2 0 so it never fires (Random(9) < 0 is never true), keeping
# the compared path RNG-free; its rotation is still fully checked.
world ORCLDEV
seed 0
phase
boot 240
capture title
play
# unpause and let the conveyors turn for a while
move right
capture devices-turning
settle 24
capture devices-settled
# walk east into the transporter at 8,13. ElementTransporterMove only accepts
# entry along the transporter's own step, and only lands the player on the first
# square past it — unless a PAIRED transporter facing back (-deltaX) re-arms the
# search, which the one at 11,13 does. So the player clears both solid squares
# and is set down past the pair.
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
settle 16
capture transported
